# CRM Reports System PRD

## Overview
The CRM Reports System is designed to provide comprehensive analytics and insights across three main modules: Deals, Quotations, and Contracts. The system will maintain consistency with the existing Vue.js 3 stack and UI/UX design patterns.

## System Architecture

### 1. Directory Structure
```
src/
├── pages/
│   └── reports/
│       ├── DealsReports.vue
│       ├── QuotationsReports.vue
│       └── ContractsReports.vue
├── components/
│   └── reports/
│       ├── filters/
│       │   ├── DateRangeFilter.vue
│       │   └── ModuleSelector.vue
│       ├── charts/
│       │   ├── LineChart.vue
│       │   ├── BarChart.vue
│       │   └── PieChart.vue
│       └── common/
│           ├── KPICard.vue
│           └── ReportListView.vue
└── stores/
    └── reports.js
```

### 2. Routing Structure
```javascript
{
  path: '/reports',
  name: 'Reports',
  children: [
    {
      path: 'deals',
      name: 'DealsReports',
      component: () => import('@/pages/reports/DealsReports.vue')
    },
    {
      path: 'quotations',
      name: 'QuotationsReports',
      component: () => import('@/pages/reports/QuotationsReports.vue')
    },
    {
      path: 'contracts',
      name: 'ContractsReports',
      component: () => import('@/pages/reports/ContractsReports.vue')
    }
  ]
}
```

## Features & Components

### 1. Global Components

#### DateRangeFilter
- Presets: Last Week, Last Month, Last Year, Custom Range
- Consistent with existing UI components
- Reactive updates to all connected reports

#### ModuleSelector
- Switch between different report modules
- Maintains selected module state
- Updates sidebar active state

### 2. Module-Specific Reports

#### A. Deals Reports
1. KPI Section
   - Total Deal Value
   - Deal Win Rate
   - Average Deal Size
   - Active Deals Count

2. Charts
   - Deal Pipeline Analysis
   - Revenue Trend
   - Territory Distribution
   - Deal Type Distribution

3. List View
   - Similar to Deals.vue list view
   - Additional analytics columns
   - Export functionality

#### B. Quotations Reports
1. KPI Section
   - Total Quote Value
   - Conversion Rate
   - Average Quote Value
   - Active Quotes Count

2. Charts
   - Quotation Status Distribution
   - Quote Value Trend
   - Product Distribution
   - Payment Terms Analysis

3. List View
   - Based on existing list view structure
   - Quote-specific metrics
   - Filterable columns

#### C. Contracts Reports
1. KPI Section
   - Active Contracts Value
   - Renewal Rate
   - Average Contract Value
   - Expiring Contracts Count

2. Charts
   - Contract Status Distribution
   - Contract Value Trend
   - Customer Segment Analysis
   - Renewal Timeline

3. List View
   - Contract-specific columns
   - Renewal tracking
   - Risk indicators

## Technical Implementation

### 1. Data Management
- Use existing Frappe backend APIs
- Implement caching for report data
- Batch loading for large datasets

### 2. State Management
- Extend existing stores pattern
- Module-specific report states
- Global filter state management

### 3. Performance Considerations
- Lazy loading of chart components
- Data pagination in list views
- Optimized re-rendering

## UI/UX Guidelines

### 1. Layout
- Consistent with existing CRM design
- Responsive grid system using Tailwind
- Mobile-first approach

### 2. Components
- Match existing component styling
- Use current color scheme
- Maintain spacing patterns

### 3. Interactions
- Smooth transitions between views
- Interactive chart tooltips
- Responsive filters

## Phase 1 Implementation Plan

1. Core Infrastructure
   - Setup routing structure
   - Create base components
   - Implement global filters

2. Deals Reports
   - Implement KPI cards
   - Create basic charts
   - Setup list view

3. Quotations Reports
   - Port deals structure
   - Customize for quotations
   - Add specific metrics

4. Contracts Reports
   - Adapt existing patterns
   - Implement contract metrics
   - Create specific views

## Success Metrics
- Report load time < 2s
- Chart interaction delay < 100ms
- List view scroll performance
- Filter response time < 500ms

## Dependencies
- Existing Vue.js 3 stack
- Frappe UI components
- Current authentication system
- Backend API endpoints

## Notes
- Maintain existing file structure
- Use current component patterns
- Follow established naming conventions
- Preserve current routing logic 